{"title":"HIPAA Compliance Setup for Healthcare Meeting Software - Complete Guide","blocks":{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"a","text":"Skip to main content","href":"#main"},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"section","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"text","text":"US Healthcare HIPAA Compliance"}]},{"type":"h1","text":"HIPAA Setup with Meetily"},{"type":"p","text":"Complete guide for US healthcare organizations to set up Meetily in HIPAA-compliant environments. Protect patient health information (PHI) with privacy-first AI meeting assistance."},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"a","text":"Buy Now","href":"/buy-now"},{"type":"button","text":"Start free trial"},{"type":"button","text":"Talk to Us"}]},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"HIPAA READY"},{"type":"li","text":"LOCAL PHI PROCESSING"},{"type":"li","text":"NO BAA REQUIRED"},{"type":"li","text":"HEALTHCARE OPTIMIZED"},{"type":"li","text":"100% LOCAL PHI PROCESSING"},{"type":"li","text":"TECHNICAL SAFEGUARDS BUILT-IN"},{"type":"li","text":"NO THIRD-PARTY DATA SHARING"}]}]},{"type":"img","src":"https://meetily.ai/home.png","alt":"Meetily HIPAA Compliance"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"section","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h2","text":"🇪🇺 European Healthcare Organizations"},{"type":"p","text":"If you're a healthcare provider in the EU, GDPR compliance is more relevant than HIPAA.HIPAA applies to US healthcare organizations, while EU healthcare must comply with GDPR Article 9 (special category data) and country-specific laws like DSGVO (Germany), RGPD (France), or national healthcare data protection regulations."},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"a","text":"View EU Healthcare GDPR Guide","href":"/guides/gdpr-compliance"},{"type":"a","text":"Healthcare Use Cases","href":"/use-cases/healthcare"},{"type":"a","text":"HIPAA Meeting Assistant","href":"/hipaa-meeting-assistant"}]},{"type":"p","text":"EU Countries Covered: Germany (DSGVO), France (RGPD + CNIL), Spain (LOPDGDD), Netherlands (UAVG), Italy (Privacy Code), and all 27 EU member states"}]}]},{"type":"section","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h2","text":"Why Meetily Works for HIPAA"},{"type":"p","text":"Local processing architecture eliminates PHI transmission risks"}]},{"type":"div","layout":"grid-3","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Local PHI Processing"},{"type":"p","text":"All meeting transcription happens locally on your devices. PHI never leaves your healthcare network, eliminating transmission risks and third-party exposure."}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"No Third-Party BAAs"},{"type":"p","text":"Since no data is processed by third parties, Business Associate Agreements (BAAs) with external vendors are not required for core functionality."}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Access Control Ready"},{"type":"p","text":"You maintain complete control over who accesses meeting transcripts. Implement role-based access and audit trails as required by HIPAA."}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Audit Trail Support"},{"type":"p","text":"Local logging of all data processing activities. Track PHI access, modifications, and deletions for compliance documentation."}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Minimum Necessary"},{"type":"p","text":"Process only required meeting audio for transcription. Built-in data minimization satisfies HIPAA's minimum necessary standard."}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Healthcare Optimized"},{"type":"p","text":"Designed for patient consultations, medical team rounds, and research meetings while keeping PHI secure and local."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"section","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h2","text":"HIPAA Safeguards Implementation"},{"type":"p","text":"How Meetily supports HIPAA Security Rule requirements"}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Technical Safeguards (§ 164.312)"},{"type":"div","layout":"grid-2","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"🔐 Access Control"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• Unique user authentication for device access"},{"type":"li","text":"• Role-based access to meeting transcripts"},{"type":"li","text":"• Automatic workstation locking"},{"type":"li","text":"• Session timeout mechanisms"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"📊 Audit Controls"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• User access logging to PHI transcripts"},{"type":"li","text":"• Meeting recording timestamps"},{"type":"li","text":"• Transcript generation and access tracking"},{"type":"li","text":"• File modification and deletion logs"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"🔧 Data Integrity"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• File system permissions (read-only after creation)"},{"type":"li","text":"• Digital signatures for transcript files"},{"type":"li","text":"• Version control for document changes"},{"type":"li","text":"• Regular backup validation"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"✅ Transmission Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Automatic Compliance: Meetily's local processing eliminates transmission security concerns - PHI is never transmitted over networks."}]}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Administrative Safeguards (§ 164.308)"},{"type":"div","layout":"grid-2","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"👤 Security Officer"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• Oversee Meetily deployment security"},{"type":"li","text":"• Monitor access to meeting transcripts"},{"type":"li","text":"• Conduct regular security assessments"},{"type":"li","text":"• Manage incident response procedures"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"🎓 Workforce Training"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• HIPAA Privacy and Security Rules overview"},{"type":"li","text":"• PHI identification in meeting contexts"},{"type":"li","text":"• Meetily proper usage procedures"},{"type":"li","text":"• Incident reporting requirements"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"⚠️ Contingency Plan"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• Regular encrypted backups of transcripts"},{"type":"li","text":"• Secure backup storage locations"},{"type":"li","text":"• Disaster recovery procedures"},{"type":"li","text":"• Business continuity planning"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"📋 Risk Assessment"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• Conduct HIPAA Security Risk Assessment"},{"type":"li","text":"• Document Meetily usage scenarios"},{"type":"li","text":"• Identify and mitigate risks"},{"type":"li","text":"• Regular compliance reviews"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h3","text":"Physical Safeguards (§ 164.310)"},{"type":"div","layout":"grid-3","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"🏢 Facility Access"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• Secured physical locations"},{"type":"li","text":"• Access card controls"},{"type":"li","text":"• Visitor escort policies"},{"type":"li","text":"• Security camera coverage"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"💻 Workstation Security"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• Laptop encryption requirements"},{"type":"li","text":"• Cable locks for desktops"},{"type":"li","text":"• Secure storage when not in use"},{"type":"li","text":"• Mobile device management"}]}]},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"h4","text":"💾 Media Controls"},{"type":"ul","children":[{"type":"li","text":"• Secure disposal of storage media"},{"type":"li","text":"• Backup tape security"},{"type":"li","text":"• USB device restrictions"},{"type":"li","text":"• Data sanitization procedures"}]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"section","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"div","childr